              "path": "check.mjs",
              "expected_sha256": "0e837f068eb50989b100cf55aa4ed7c9e9101fb219ac6d9c7ec40ea673a684c4",
              "actual_sha256": "0e837f068eb50989b100cf55aa4ed7c9e9101fb219ac6d9c7ec40ea673a684c4"
            }
          ],
          "content": "## Mechanism\n`isAdult(age)` follows this path: `age` → JavaScript runtime `Number.isInteger(age)` → short-circuited inclusive comparison `age >= 18` → Boolean. If `Number.isInteger(age)` is false, `&&` short-circuits and returns false without evaluating the comparison. Otherwise, `age >= 18` returns a Boolean, so the function always returns a Boolean.\n\n## Invalid values and effects\nStrings, `NaN`, infinities, fractional values, and other non-integers return false. Integer ages below 18 also return false. The function has no state changes or I/O, raises no errors for these invalid values, and uses no external packages.\n\n## Testing and maintenance\nThe configured `age-boundaries` check covers 17, 18, 19, a string, `NaN`, infinity, and a fractional age. Run it after changing `isAdult`. If the age threshold or accepted input type changes, update the check and this note together.",
